menu "BTClock data source"

config BTCLOCK_WATCHDOG_FAST_FOR_TEST
    bool "Use short watchdog timings (development/testing only)"
    default n
    help
      When enabled, the BtclockDataSource staleness watchdog uses
      development-friendly short timings:
        - Tick: 20 s (production: 5 min)
        - Stale threshold: 60 s (production: 60 min)

      This is for local fault-injection testing (e.g. against a modified
      backend that artificially drops the blockheight subscription) so a
      full failure → detect → recover cycle fits in ~2 minutes instead of
      ~70. Production firmware MUST leave this off — short timings would
      trigger a reconnect on every natural >60 s block-interval gap.

      See bd btclock_v4-lfd for the watchdog implementation.

endmenu
